ct value.\n\nReason: \n\nI have trip tens, which is a very strong hand on this board. My opponent's moderate betting (300-300) suggests they likely have a good but not great hand - possibly top pair, two pair, or a draw. By raising to 600-1000, I accomplish multiple goals: (1) protect my hand against flush and straight draws by making it expensive for them to chase, (2) extract value if they have a weaker made hand like top pair, and (3) potentially take down the pot immediately. Calling would be too passive and allows draws to see the river cheaply. Going all-in might be too aggressive and fold out hands I can extract value from. A solid raise of 1000 chips represents strength while still giving them a chance to make a mistake.\n\nAnswer: 1000"}
