00.\nYour valid actions are: [-2 (All-in), -1 (Fold), 0 (Check), 4000 (raise the bet), or any value above 4000 but lower than your current chips.].\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Evaluation:\n\nLet me analyze this situation carefully:\n\n**My Hand:** 10 of Diamonds, 10 of Clubs\n**Board:** King of Diamonds, 5 of Spades, Queen of Diamonds, 10 of Spades\n\n**Current Hand Strength:**\nI have Three of a Kind (10s) - a very strong hand on the turn. Specifically, I have trip 10s with K-Q kickers.\n\n**Betting Analysis:**\n- Round 0 (Pre-flop): I raised 200, opponent called\n- Round 1 (Flop): Opponent bet 300, I called\n- Round 2 (Turn): Opponent bet 300, I raised to 1000, opponent re-raised to 2000\n\nThe opponent has shown significant aggression with a re-raise on the turn. \n\n**Possible Opponent Hands to Consider:**\n1. **Two Pair or better:** K-Q (two pair), K-10, Q-10 (though I have two 10s)\n2. **Straight draw:** J-9 would give an open-ended straight draw\n3. **Flush draw:** Two diamonds would give a flush draw (3 diamonds on board)\n4. **Made straight:** J-9 would make a straight (K-Q-J-10-9) - this is very dangerous\n5. **Bluff/Semi-bluff:** Overplaying a pair or draw\n\n**Risk Assessment:**\n- The only hand that currently beats me is a straight (J-9)\n- A flush draw or straight draw could complete on the river\n- I'm ahead of all pairs, two pairs, and most other combinations\n\n**Chip Situation:**\n- I have 18,400 chips (started with 20,000)\n- I'm ahead cumulatively by 1,750 chips\n- Pot is getting large with the re-raise to 2000\n\n**Strategic Options:**\n1. **Fold (-1):** Too weak given my trip 10s\n2. **Call (0):** See the river cheaply, but allows opponent to realize equity\n3. **Raise (4000+):** Apply pressure, but commits more chips\n4. **All-in (-2):** Maximum pressure, but risky if opponent has the straight\n\nGiven I have three of a kind (strong hand) and only a straight beats me currently, calling seems reasonable to control pot size and see the river